# identity.rules — the commit identity rule, in ONE place. The clone's pre-commit and pre-push, tools/preflight-public.sh,
# the lane's publish gate and the added-lines gate all read it, the hooks from HEAD (a commit cannot loosen the rule that
# judges it; the first commit of a repository, with no HEAD yet, reads the staged copy — never the working tree).
# Two keys, each one extended regex (grep -E / bash [[ =~ ]]), matched against the identity git RECORDS for the author AND
# the committer (so --author, `git -c` and the GIT_* variables count):
#   email     the whole address must match
#   name_bad  what a name may NOT be: an address, a hostname, a dotted quad (names are handles)
# A value is ONE token: whitespace around it is trimmed, whitespace inside it refuses. A repository that commits under another
# address edits the `email` line only. A missing key, a regex that does not compile or CR line endings refuse every commit
# (fail closed) — see .gitattributes.
email ^[0-9]+\+[A-Za-z0-9-]+@users\.noreply\.github\.com$
name_bad @|\.(local|lan|home|internal|arpa)\.?$|\.ts\.net\.?$|^[0-9]{1,3}(\.[0-9]{1,3}){3}\.?$
